Sentence 1: Sprechgesang
Sprechgesang ' (, "spoken singing") and ' (, "spoken voice") are expressionist vocal techniques between singing and speaking.
Sentence 2: Though sometimes used interchangeably, "Sprechgesang" is directly related to the operatic "recitative" manner of singing (in which pitches are sung, but the articulation is rapid and loose like speech), whereas "Sprechstimme" is closer to speech itself (because it does not emphasise any particular pitches).
Sentence 3: "Sprechgesang" is more closely aligned with the long-used musical techniques of "recitative" or "parlando" than is "Sprechstimme".
