Sentence 2: They are prostrate, perennial, herbaceous plants, with creeping stems which take root readily at the leaf nodes.
Sentence 3: Many of these plants are economically valuable food crops and ornamentals and cannot be sold if they are infected or damaged by stem and bulb nematodes.
