Sentence 1: Plectranthus
Plectranthus Plectranthus, with some 350 species, is a genus of warm-climate plants occurring largely in the southern hemisphere, in sub-Saharan Africa, Madagascar, India and the Indonesian archipelago down to Australia and some Pacific Islands.
Sentence 2: "Plectranthus" species are used as food plants by the larvae of some Lepidoptera species including The Engrailed ("Ectropis crepuscularia").
