Sentence 1: German Longhaired Pointer
German Longhaired Pointer The German longhaired pointer (GLP) is a breed of dog.
Sentence 2: Developed in Germany, it is used as a multipurpose gundog.
Sentence 3: As with many breeds bred for work, they are not generally kept as a companion dog and do not make good pets; they require a lot of space and exercise, and can be dominant and destructive.
Sentence 4: German Wirehaired Pointer The German Wirehaired Pointer is a medium to large-sized griffon type breed of dog developed in the 19th century in Germany for hunting.
Sentence 5: It became a leading gun dog in Germany in the later part of the 20th century.
Sentence 6: The German Wirehaired pointer is a well muscled, medium to large-sized dog of distinctive appearance.
