Sentence 1: Asian migrant brides in Japan
Asian migrant brides in Japan The increasing number of Asian migrant brides in Japan () marrying Japanese men is a phenomenon occurring in both rural and urban Japan.
Sentence 2: Since the mid 1980s, rural Japanese men have begun taking foreign Asian brides, from the Philippines, Sri Lanka, Thailand, China and South Korea, as a way of countering the reduced number of women who are of marriageable, childbearing age that are willing to marry rural Japanese men.
Sentence 3: During the 1980s and 1990s, local authorities started government-led initiatives encouraging marriage between women from other Asian countries and Japanese farmers due to the lack of Japanese women who wanted to live in the countryside.
Sentence 4: These Asian brides came from the Philippines, Sri Lanka, Thailand, China and South Korea.
