Sentence 2: The genus name "Ammophila" originates from the Greek words ἄμμος ("ámmos"), meaning "sand", and φίλος ("philos"), meaning "friend".
Sentence 3: The "Ammophila" grasses are widely known as examples of xerophytes, plants that can withstand dry conditions.
Sentence 4: Despite their occurrence on seacoasts, "Ammophila" grasses are not particularly tolerant of saline soils; they can tolerate a salinity of about 15 g/l (1.5%), which makes them "moderate halophytes".
Sentence 5: "Ammophila" builds coastal sand dunes and thus stabilizes the sand.
