Sentence 1: Hindustani grammar
Hindustani grammar Hindustani, the lingua franca of northern India and Pakistan, has two standardised registers: Hindi and Urdu.
Sentence 2: Grammatically differences between the two standards are minor but each uses its own script: Hindi uses Devanagari while Urdu uses an extended form of the Perso-Arabic script, typically in the Nastaʿlīq style.
Sentence 3: Hindustani language
