Sentence 1: Cotoneaster integerrimus
Cotoneaster integerrimus Cotoneaster integerrimus, the common cotoneaster, is a species of "Cotoneaster" native to central and eastern Europe and southwest Asia, from southern Belgium and eastern France south to Italy, and east through Germany to the Balkans, northern Turkey, the Crimea, the Caucasus and northern Iran; plants in Spain may also belong in this species.
Sentence 2: In the past, it was treated in a wider sense, including plants from Wales now split off as "Cotoneaster cambricus" and plants from Scandinavia now treated as "Cotoneaster scandinavicus", but differs from these in genetic profile and detail of foliage and fruit.
