Sentence 3: Furthermore, as maximum RPM increases, higher spring force is required to prevent valve float, leading to increased cam drag and higher wear on the parts at all speeds, problems addressed by the desmodromic mechanism.
Sentence 4: Desmodromic valve
Desmodromic valve A desmodromic valve is a reciprocating engine poppet valve that is positively closed by a cam and leverage system, rather than by a more conventional spring.
Sentence 5: In a conventional four-stroke engine valves are opened by a cam and closed by return spring.
Sentence 6: An engine using desmodromic valves has two cams and two actuators, each for positive opening and closing without a return spring.
