Sentence 1: Bromeliaceae
Bromeliaceae The Bromeliaceae (the bromeliads) are a family of monocot flowering plants of 51 genera and around 3475 known species native mainly to the tropical Americas, with a few species found in the American subtropics and one in tropical west Africa, "Pitcairnia feliciana".
Sentence 2: Lennooideae
