Sentence 3: It was traditionally treated at family rank as Lennoaceae, and placed in different orders by different authors, including Lamiales (in the Cronquist system) and Solanales (Dahlgren system).
Sentence 4: Taxonomy for this genus is currently being reanalysed, with the genus "Hebe" and the related Australasian genera "Derwentia", "Detzneria", "Chionohebe", "Heliohebe", "Leonohebe" and "Parahebe" now included by many botanists.
Sentence 5: Monophyly of the genus is supported by nuclear ribosomal internal
